# TEMPLATE ONLY - production; intentionally no active assignments for Selenium.
# Selenium does NOT require Supabase keys, DATABASE_URL or LLM provider keys.
# Run CLI with --mode selenium explicitly; default CLI mode is browser-use.
# Browser mode, limits and output directory are CLI/job parameters, not env keys.
# Keep output/checkpoint storage persistent and separate for production.
# Dynamic keywords/portals/schedules belong to backend workflow configuration.
# Queue/internal API access settings are pending the cross-container integration contract.
# APP_ENV is NOT currently read by the crawler; environment identity must come from
# deployment/service naming until application support is implemented.
# See specs-careeros/ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES.md.

# Shared global execution capacity; replicate workers separately for parallel runs.
CRAWLER_MAX_CONCURRENCY=1
